Apple today <a href="https://www.apple.com/in/newsroom/2026/11/apple-rolls-out-all-new-map-across-india/">announced</a> the rollout of an all-new Apple Maps experience in India, bringing the company's redesigned map to the country for the first time. The update offers faster and more accurate navigation, more detailed views of roads, buildings, parks, and shopping centers, and over 300 three-dimensional landmarks.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/Apple-Maps-India-3up-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="2560" height="1440" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1078084" /><br/>
Notably, the new enhanced map includes features built specifically for India. For example, Natural Language Guidance, which gives directions in conversational phrases such as "At the next traffic light, turn left," has been enhanced with real-world details like pillars and other points of interest. The idea is for Maps to be able to guide users along roads that have no names with directions like "Turn right after the petrol pump." <br/>
<br/>
Elsewhere, dual-language labels show place names in both English and the local language of a region, just like the country's road signs. Alongside English and Hindi, Apple Maps has added support for Bengali, Gujarati, Kannada, Malayalam, Marathi, Tamil, Telugu, Punjabi, Odia, and Urdu.<br/>
<br/>
The rollout also brings Look Around to India for the first time, giving users anywhere in the world interactive street-level imagery with high-resolution 3D photography. It also adds AR Walking Directions, which overlay step-by-step guidance onto the real world when users raise their iPhone.<br/>
<br/>
Other features now available in India include lane guidance, multi-stop routing for up to 15 stops with routes that sync from Mac and iPad to iPhone, Share ETA, cycling directions with elevation details, and electric vehicle routing that can plan trips around charging stops. Users can also report accidents, hazards, and speed checks hands-free by telling Siri AI. <br/>
<br/>
Lastly, transit riders in Ahmedabad, Bengaluru, Chennai, Delhi, Hyderabad, Kolkata, Mumbai, and Pune (as well as on Indian Railways) can use Apple Maps to plan journeys, find nearby stations, and get notifications when it's time to get off at their stop.<br/>
<blockquote>"Apple Maps is the best way to explore and navigate the world, and we are excited to bring an enhanced Maps experience to even more users with today's rollout of the new map in India," said Max Muller, Apple's VP of Apple Maps. "The new map offers some of our users' favourite features like Look Around and AR Walking Directions, but we've also designed the map for India's specific navigation needs, including enhanced Natural Language Guidance and customized dual-language labels, making it easier than ever for users to find the places they love and get to where they're going."</blockquote>The redesigned Apple Maps first launched in the United States in 2018 and has <a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/2026/01/2025-marked-a-record-breaking-year-for-apple-services/#:~:text=Additionally%2C%20Maps%20brought,directions%2C%20and%20more.">expanded to more countries</a> in the years since, but India has remained a notable gap, despite Apple opening a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2016/05/19/apple-hyderabad-maps-development/">Maps-focused development center in Hyderabad</a> back in 2016. Turn-by-turn navigation only <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2019/01/10/apple-maps-gains-turn-by-turn-directions-india/">arrived in the country in 2019</a>.<br/>
<br/>
